.TH MICROIDE 1 "2026-06-18" "microide" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
microide \- compact native desktop IDE shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B microide
[\fB--disable-plugins\fR] [\fB--safe-mode\fR] [\fB--control-spec\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fIproject-path\fR]
.br
.B microide control-help
.br
.B microide control-commands
.br
.B microide control-list
.br
.B microide dump-state
.I persisted-file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B microide
is a single-window desktop editor and IDE shell (editor, compare, merge,
search, git, terminal, plugin, and debugger workflows). With no
.I project-path
it opens the current working directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --disable-plugins
Start without loading the Lua plugin runtime.
.TP
.B --safe-mode
Start without plugins and without restoring the previous session.
.TP
.B --control-spec \fIfile\fR
Apply a cold-start control spec at launch: open a project with breakpoints
already set (and optionally reveal files / start a debug session) before the
window becomes interactive. The spec's
.I project
field, when present, selects the project to open. See
.B microide control-help
for the JSON schema. Spec line numbers are 1-based; relative paths resolve
against the project root.
.SH CONTROL CHANNEL
An external tool (such as an LLM) can drive a running instance over a private
Unix-domain socket: set breakpoints (including conditional, hit-count and
logpoint), step through a debug session, open/close files, switch projects,
open terminals, and observe where execution stopped.
.PP
The channel is OFF by default. Enable the
.B control.enabled
setting (Settings overlay, Ctrl+, or the
.B settings
command); it starts immediately on the running instance with no restart. The
socket is created mode 0600 under
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/microide/ ,
and a descriptor file is written to
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/microide/instances/<pid>.json .
.PP
Requests and responses are newline-delimited JSON. A request is either
.RB { \(dqcommand\(dq : \(dq...\(dq }
(run any command \(em see
.BR "microide control-commands" )
or
.RB { \(dqquery\(dq : \(dq...\(dq }
(read state: \fBdebug-state\fR, \fBbreakpoints\fR, \fBtabs\fR, \fBprojects\fR,
\fBstatus\fR). The server also pushes unsolicited \fBstopped\fR, \fBterminated\fR
and \fBoutput\fR events so a client can wait for execution to stop.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B control-help
Print the full control-channel protocol, query verbs, spec schema, and the list
of runnable commands.
.TP
.B control-commands
Print every runnable command name and its usage.
.TP
.B control-list
Print the descriptor of each running instance that has the control channel
enabled (pid, socket path, project).
.TP
.B dump-state \fIpersisted-file\fR
Decode and print a microide persisted-state file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/microide/<pid>.sock
Per-instance control socket (mode 0600).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/microide/instances/<pid>.json
Per-instance discovery descriptor.
.SH SECURITY
The control channel grants a connecting client the same power as the command
palette. It is off by default, the socket is user-private (0600) under the
per-user runtime directory, and it must be explicitly enabled per instance.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation under \fIdev-docs/\fR, in particular
\fIdev-docs/control/control-channel.md\fR and
\fIdev-docs/debugger/dap-integration.md\fR.
